    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_h033",
        "cnm_152"
      ],
      "explanation": "Take any \\(0\\le x_1<x_2\\). Factoring the output difference makes its sign clear:\n\\[\nx_2^2-x_1^2=(x_2-x_1)(x_2+x_1)>0.\n\\]\nBoth factors are positive because \\(x_2>x_1\\ge0\\). Thus the larger input always has the larger output on \\([0,+\\infty)\\), so the function is increasing. The answer is A.",
      "id": "definition-and-factorization",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_h032_q4#definition-and-factorization",
      "title": "Compare two arbitrary outputs"
